### Step 5: Multi-Tenant Cross-Namespace Pod Isolation Drill

Practice combining `namespaceSelector` and `podSelector` (logical AND) to restrict traffic between tenant namespaces
under strict default-deny isolation:

```bash
# 1. Deploy tenant-a, tenant-b, isolated workloads, and default-deny policies
kubectl apply -f 06-cross-tenant-workloads.yaml

# 2. Verify baseline isolation (both frontend and analytics pods time out)
kubectl exec deploy/frontend-app -n {{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_a | default('tenant-a') }} -- \
  curl -s -m 3 "http://db-service.{{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_b | default('tenant-b') }}:5432" || echo "Frontend blocked!"
kubectl exec deploy/analytics-worker -n {{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_a | default('tenant-a') }} -- \
  curl -s -m 3 "http://db-service.{{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_b | default('tenant-b') }}:5432" || echo "Analytics blocked!"

# 3. Apply selective cross-namespace policies (logical AND)
kubectl apply -f 07-allow-cross-tenant.yaml

# 4. Verify selective reachability:
# Authorized frontend succeeds (returns "PostgreSQL Mock 5432 OK")
kubectl exec deploy/frontend-app -n {{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_a | default('tenant-a') }} -- \
  curl -s -m 5 "http://db-service.{{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_b | default('tenant-b') }}:5432"

# Unauthorized analytics pod remains blocked (podSelector enforcement)
kubectl exec deploy/analytics-worker -n {{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_a | default('tenant-a') }} -- \
  curl -s -m 3 "http://db-service.{{ cka_lab_networking_tenant_b | default('tenant-b') }}:5432" || echo "Analytics blocked!"

# 5. Run automated test runner
./test-cross-tenant.sh
```

